.TH elfshaker-show 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-show \- Write files from a snapshot to standard output.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker show\fR [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISNAPSHOT\fR> <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes the selected snapshot files to standard output in command\-line order. When multiple paths are given, their contents are concatenated without separators. The command fails without producing output if any requested path is absent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISNAPSHOT\fR>
Snapshot tag or PACK:SNAPSHOT identifier to read.
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path within the snapshot to write.
